# MASTER PROMPT — Complete TechVantage BD Course Selling Platform

Build a complete, premium, production-oriented online course-selling website for **TechVantage BD**, targeting customers in Bangladesh.

This must be a real, functional web application, not just a landing page, UI mockup, prototype, or collection of non-functional buttons.

The platform must support account-free course browsing, guest checkout, bKash/Nagad manual payment verification, administrator-controlled Telegram access, secure order tracking and recovery, a hidden administrator entry point, full website content management, course image uploads, and a premium blurred video-style course gallery.

## 1. First Inspect the Project

Before writing code, inspect the existing workspace and identify:

- Existing frontend and backend frameworks.
- Current database schema and migrations.
- Existing checkout, order tracking, and course-access logic.
- Current administrator authentication and permissions.
- Telegram integration and environment variables.
- Existing reusable components, routes, tests, and configuration.

If an existing application is present, improve it without unnecessarily replacing its architecture or deleting working features.

If the workspace is empty, create a complete application using a maintainable TypeScript frontend, a secure server-side API, and Supabase PostgreSQL for persistent data and authentication. Choose a compatible framework based on the available environment and deployment target.

Do not create a frontend-only application that stores orders or administrator credentials in browser storage.

