## 16. Testing and Acceptance Criteria

Implement meaningful automated tests and run them.

Test at least:

### Public Website
- Homepage renders correctly.
- Course gallery displays blurred images and centered lock icons.
- Course cards open the appropriate details or checkout.
- Responsive layouts work at common screen sizes.
- Footer copyright text is exact.

### Guest Checkout
- Customers can browse and purchase without registering.
- Valid package prices are server-authoritative.
- Tampered package IDs or prices are rejected.
- Required fields are validated.
- Duplicate transaction IDs are rejected.
- Concurrent checkout submissions cannot bypass duplicate protection.

### Order Tracking and Recovery
- Valid private tokens work.
- Incorrect, malformed, and unauthorized tokens fail.
- An order ID alone does not reveal private details.
- Customers cannot access another customer's order.
- Phone-number recovery requires verified ownership.
- Recovery rate limits and expiry rules work.

### Administrator
- Clicking `©` opens the PIN dialog.
- Incorrect PINs are rejected.
- PIN verification is server-side.
- Correct PIN alone does not grant administrator permissions.
- Direct unauthorized requests to admin APIs fail.
- Admin changes persist after refresh.
- Image uploads and replacements work.
- Payment approval and rejection are recorded.
- Unauthorized visitors cannot modify website settings.

### Telegram
- Pending orders never reveal a usable invitation.
- Rejected orders never receive invitations.
- Approved orders can generate real invitations when valid credentials and permissions are available.
- Failed Telegram requests are reported accurately.
- Repeated requests do not generate conflicting links.
- Invitation recovery follows the secure verification flow.

### Entitlements
- Pending and rejected orders cannot unlock paid lessons.
- Approved orders receive the correct entitlement.
- Thirty-day and ninety-day access expires according to server time.
- Lifetime access does not expire accidentally.
- Expired access is rejected.
- Protected lesson content cannot be obtained simply by calling public APIs.

